            <ArticleTitle>An unusual cause of lower back pain: uterus didelphys and unilateral cervical atresia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>125-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Backache among adolescents and young women is an unusual presenting feature to the Accident and Emergency Department as well as orthopaedic clinics. Here, we present a challenging case of a mullerian duct abnormality, which collectively has an incidence of 0.0001% of the population, and how its consideration and investigation will ensure optimum management in both acute and long-term.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
